<!--
  Every entry below is one deliberate break, and all of them are the same break: the
  constants that used to be named UPPER_CASE were renamed to PascalCase so the whole
  family follows one convention (#298). Forty-two members across three target frameworks,
  every one of them CP0002 (the member no longer exists). Forty-one are a public or
  protected `const` that kept its value and its meaning and changed only its spelling.
  The forty-second is XorFilter's instance `FingerprintBits` property, which could not
  survive its own constant being renamed onto the same name, and was redundant with it.

  Callers migrate mechanically: DEFAULT_CAPACITY becomes DefaultCapacity, MIN_PRECISION
  becomes MinPrecision, FINGERPRINT_BITS becomes FingerprintBits, and
  `filter.FingerprintBits` becomes `XorFilter<T, THasher>.FingerprintBits`.

  `scripts/check_constant_naming.js` keeps the convention from drifting back, so this file
  should not need to grow for this reason again. All of it can be deleted once
  CelerityPackageValidationBaseline moves past the release that carries the rename.
-->
